LabelRollHint = Label printer mode: each label prints as its own %s × %s mm page. In the print dialog choose the matching label size (the browser will usually preselect it) and print at full scale, not fit-to-page.
LabelRollNeedsHeight = Label printer mode needs a label height so each page matches the label stock — set Height in the layout (0 = auto only works for sheets).
LabelSecShow = Show
LabelWidth = Width
LabelHeight = Height
LabelHeightHint = 0 = automatic height
LabelPadTopHint = Extra top padding leaves a blank strip at the top of every label, e.g. 21 mm for slide-in bin holders
LabelFontBody = Body
LabelFontCorner = Corner tag
LabelCornerHint = 0 = hide. Rule of thumb: character height in cm ≈ reading distance in cm ÷ 200 (2 m → ~1 cm ≈ 28 pt)
LabelBorder = Border (mm)
