#
# CSV import/export
#
CsvImportExport = Import/Export
CsvPageDesc = CSV round-trip for spreadsheet workflows (Google Sheets, Excel): export, edit, download as CSV, import. Imports show a preview of every planned change before anything is written, and apply all-or-nothing.
CsvLayoutSection = Warehouse layout (levels and allowed values)
CsvLayoutDesc = Columns: warehouse; level; label; type (text/number/list/letter); allowed_values (pipe-separated, e.g. A|B|C). One row per level. Import matches levels by label, creates new ones, adds missing allowed values — it never deletes anything. For type "letter", put a single end code in allowed_values (e.g. Z, or AC to go past Z) to generate the whole A..end range in one row — a pipe-separated list is still taken as literal codes.
CsvAssignSection = Bin assignments (product → bin)
CsvAssignDesc = Per warehouse. Columns: product; product_label (ignored); lot; one column per level label; note. Level columns present in the file are authoritative — an empty cell clears that level, a fully empty row removes the assignment. Rows are matched on product ref + lot.
CsvExportAllLayouts = Export all layouts (CSV)
CsvExportAssignments = Export assignments (CSV)
